From c08de17305e7eb0038d061731b33cbe49ab14ed5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jacob Root <jacob@otisroot.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 16:04:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(vmm): a vcpu_pins entry may be a list of host CPUs

A pin could only be one host CPU. That is the right shape for CPUs set
aside for the guest, and the only one threads_per_core = 2 and dedicated
can keep their promises with, but it leaves out a placement between a pin
and the shared cpu_affinity set: each vCPU on a core of its own, free to
run on either of that core's threads. Such a vCPU still has a core no
other vCPU of the box is placed on, and when the host puts a task on one
thread it can take the other rather than wait.

An entry is now a CPU or a list of CPUs (serde untagged): `[8, [9, 25]]`.
A config of plain numbers parses as before and writes back as numbers.
A list must name at least one CPU; single CPUs still may not repeat, while
lists may overlap, since they place rather than reserve. threads_per_core
= 2 and dedicated now require one CPU in every entry, which is what they
always relied on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0119BJfiAjA3VRAtdz3uU35x
